{"lines":"222","clause":"L3.2-zero-beta","page":"UNCHECKED","status":"PASS","repair":"REPAIRS item 7","derivation":"If beta_i=0 then w_i=0, so the corresponding factor is z-independent and <=1. Any number of such factors may be dropped. For beta_i>0, row norms of an orthogonal-column matrix give beta_i<=1 and the normalized rows form the Brascamp-Lieb frame.","objective_id":"QFORM-FIVE-270-REPAIRED-AUDIT-20260925","source_commit":"4e530247ec0ef4101a6e5ecf621bd35a969c42aa","source_blob":"98e45d53d106db9a205051a4dd4917fc39dc2e3a","account":"account03","slot":"B05","run_id":"20260925T104151Z-account03-B05-five270-repaired-r01"}
